+## Built State (F043, 2026-09-30)
+
+What exists on disk at the close of F043, built on `feature/f043-explanation-layer`, cut from
+`main` at `21bfc188`. Every DECISION named lives in `.agent/decisions.md`; every round's verdict in
+`.agent/live_review.md` or, once rotated, its archive.
+
+**T001 — the catalog, the term and its tooltip.** `apps/ui/src/api/terminology.ts` holds
+`TERM_CATALOG`, the one home of every explanation: each entry a title, a plain-language body of at
+most 240 characters, the file that defines the term and a phrase that file states.
+`terminology.test.ts` reads every such file back and fails when its phrase is gone, which is how the
+catalog quotes a single source without copying it (DECISION F043 D1).
+`apps/ui/src/components/term/Term.tsx` wraps a word, writes its key into `data-term`, and opens a
+glass tooltip portalled into the page body, at once on keyboard focus and after 120 ms on hover; a
+term inside a button opens on hover only (D2), and a tile's live breakdown shows under the
+explanation (D3). The terms cover the live-status pill, the timeline's phases, the metrics bar's
+tiles, the right panel's cards, the task list's states, the NowCard's Live badge and the graph's
+SCRUBBED badge. The timeline's hint map and the metrics bar's own tooltip are deleted, since the
+term replaced them.
+
+**T002 — the audit.** `apps/ui/src/api/terminologyAudit.ts` reads the `data-term` values of rendered
+markup and answers the terms the catalog lacks and the keys nothing renders.
+`components/term/termAudit.test.ts` renders the real right panel, the metrics bar, the pill in each
+state and the timeline, requires both directions empty, and holds two drift fixtures red; the graph
+stage, which cannot load outside a browser, holds its one term through a check of its source (D1,
+D2).
+
+**T003 — the Terms panel, the tour and the end-to-end.** The question mark key, outside a text field,
+and the right panel's Terms button open `components/term/TermPanel.tsx`: every entry with its place
+and its body under a search field (D3). `components/tour/TourFrame.tsx` is the overlay engine the
+result tour now renders through and the first-run tour uses too; `components/tour/FirstRunTour.tsx`
+walks six steps, each spotting its region, opens by itself once per browser, records any way of
+ending it under `remedy:first-run-tour`, and starts again from the Terms panel; the palette's step is
+the Terms button until F044 builds a palette (D4). `tests/ui_server/test_explanation_layer_live.py`
+runs a real demo job, builds the cockpit into its own folder, and proves in headless Chrome that
+every term on the real page is in the catalog, that a planted unknown term is caught, and the tour's,
+the tooltip's and the panel's behaviour (D5). `docs/guides/explanation-layer-user-guide-v1.md`
+explains all of it for a user.
+
+**Findings.** R-1115, a tooltip detail that rendered inline so its separator never showed, was raised
+at round 3's gate and repaired in round 4.
